# CPU-write widening switch (27 Nov): a write the CPU makes to watched memory invalidates up to 256 KB around it (the
# SDK's choice: fewer faults for games that write big buffers). At 007's explosions that was ~240 faults a frame
# invalidating ~15,000 pages, and the renderer then re-uploaded and re-protected pages one or two at a time (~1,300
# protects a frame, ~2 us each). BOTS_GFX_INVALIDATION_PAGES=1/2/4/8/16/32 widens to that many pages (an aligned group,
# never over GPU-written pages) instead of 64; 1 = only the written pages. Unset or 64: unchanged. For A/B with the
# native renderer's "memory sync per frame" profile (BOTS_DRAW_PROFILE=1).
 src/graphics/shared_memory.cpp | 26 +++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 25 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

